<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5428"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 12:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->And there is a Coleman connection, yes. That&#39;s a pretty good thought, Lilymarie. The Otero letter indicates more than one type of rope or rope-like binding material...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
