<!--Post: 5514--><!--Time: 1107153834-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5514"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiquitah<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiquitah<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 10:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry Dorothy....Just the way you said a few things, thats all. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5514-->
<!--Post: 5887--><!--Time: 1107444153-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5887"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kayjay<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kayjay<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 7:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK said to Kevin, something like &#34;havn&#39;t I seen you at the university?&#34; IF BTK worked at Colemans, could it be that that is where he knew Kevins face from? Kevin was only at Colemans for a short period and may never have remembered seeing BTK. How often does it happen that we see a face and struggle to remember where we know it from? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5887-->
<!--Post: 7135--><!--Time: 1108224167-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7135"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 8:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I worked at the Coleman Co in the early 80&#39;s in the offices off of 2nd &amp; St. Francis. I met Sheldon Coleman Sr. before his passing, and he was very personable. I also have family members that worked at Coleman for several years. I in fact, bowled on the Coleman bowling league. I bowled with two or three people mentioned throughout different posting on this board. I&#39;ve ran through my mind and asked family members about any relevance to wierd people that we came into contact with, only one or two stand out. Nothing to go running to the WPD about. My question is to Audreyam, do you know when they started manufacturing clothesline?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7135-->
<!--Post: 9258--><!--Time: 1109451488-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9258"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sjforcum<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sjforcum<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 12:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Turns out there was a coleman connection... <BR> <BR>&#34;Other information about Rader was sketchy, but the Wichita Eagle reported that he had worked had worked for the Coleman camping gear firm in the early 1970s -- as did two of BTK&#39;s early victims. He also apparently lived on the same street as one of his victims, according to media reports.&#34; <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.msnbc.msn.com/id/7036219/" target=_top>http://www.msnbc.msn.com/id/7036219/</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9258-->
<!--Post: 9328--><!--Time: 1109477516-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9328"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whatthehell<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whatthehell<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 8:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->hey read the not real serial killer post. <BR>i believe the connection is very strong. may even hold the key to why it all started. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9328-->
<!--Post: 9518--><!--Time: 1109543927-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9518"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brady<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brady<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 2:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is another article from Kansas.com saying Dennis Rader worked at Coleman from 1971 to 1973 as an assembler.  The article also says he worked at ADT Security Services from 1974 until 1989, a chilling time period.  It seems like this is how he gained access to the victim&#39;s homes so easily: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/11004728.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/11004728.htm</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9518-->
<!--Post: 9639--><!--Time: 1109575487-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9639"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->J_eric<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->J_eric<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 11:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Congratulations, Wichitaboy, you got the winning Lottery ticket on this one!  A job as Wichita Dog Catcher awaits you.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9639-->
<!--Post: 9793--><!--Time: 1109642724-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9793"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:blingbling1169@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cawichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cawichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 6:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I really want to commend Wichita Boy! You were on point and while I hit on a few things, most were clues I chose to focus on that in the end came to be correct, you were goooood!!! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9793-->
<!--Post: 9840--><!--Time: 1109658683-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9840"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 10:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wow! Brady wrote: &#34;Dennis Rader worked at Coleman from 1971 to 1973 as an assembler.&#34; <BR> <BR>Amazing, since BLT&#39;s 1st 2 murder scenes had victims that were ALSO &#34;assembly-line workers&#34; at Coleman around 1973! <BR> <BR>The Wichita cops better have a good answer for not ID&#39;ing Denny at this time!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9840-->
<!--Post: 9921--><!--Time: 1109705337-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9921"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whatthehell<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whatthehell<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 11:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 6:18 pm:      <BR>coleman connection stats of significance <BR>we will see if it is of any accuracy <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR>A AGREE ON THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH A RATIO IN A SMALLER TOWN BUT THE WICHITA POPULATION IS FAR TOO BIG TO HAVE THAT RATIO NOT BE SIGNIFICANT. THAT IS JUST THE WORK RATIO, CONSIDER THE ODDS OF TWO PEOPLE BEING KILLED AND TWO OTHERS BEING SHOT ALL IN THE SAME FOUR MONTH PERIOD. EVEN WITH TODAYS POPULATION AND OUR NATIONAL AVERAGE OF 4 HOMICIEDS PER EVERY 10,000 PEOPLE ALLOWING FOR 2.57 PEOPLE TO BE KILLED IN WICHITA ON AVERAGE PER MONTH AND BEING 134 PER YEAR. <a href="http://www.nationmaster.com/graph-T/cri_mur_cap" target=_top>http://www.nationmaster.com/graph-T/cri_mur_cap</a>  <BR>I DO NOT KNOW HOW MANY THE COLEMAN COMPANY EMPLOYEED IN 1974 BUT TODAY IT IS 1300 AT WICHITA. THAT TRANSLATES TO AN AVERAGE MURDER RATE OF ABOUT .067 MURDERS A YEAR FOR THE COLEMAN EMPLOYEE POPULATION. SO I WOULD THINK THAT STATISTICALLY 2 MURDERS AND TWO SHOOTING IN 4 MONTHS WOULD BE OF A VERY HIGH SIGNIFICANCE.  <BR>THE RATIO OF COLEMAN EMPLOYEES 1300 TO THE GENERAL WICHITA POPULATION 336,300 IS ABOUT 1 IN EVERY 259 PEOPLE.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9921-->
<!--Post: 9923--><!--Time: 1109705471-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9923"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whatthehell<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whatthehell<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 11:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have agreed with you since the beginning wichitaboy. Vscantu asks a good question, surely the coleman and wsy hits both on DR raised a flag back in the 74. We will probably never know.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9923-->
<!--Post: 9927--><!--Time: 1109706024-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9927"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 11:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whatthehell - As always I appreicate you! And, yes we were both right in believeing that there was a Coleman connection. Unfortunately, nobody I knew was acquainted with Rader!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9927-->
<!--Post: 10095--><!--Time: 1109751927-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10095"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 12:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Coleman did a search of their archived records and it shows that Dennis Rader was an employee with them from June 19, 1972 until July 6, 1973.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10095-->
<!--Post: 10110--><!--Time: 1109769888-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10110"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 5:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Excellent research, JOHNO! Now, we just have to compare BLTs&#39; dates of work at Coleman with those of his 3 victims who ALSO WORKED AT COLEMAN: 1&#41; Julie Otero  2&#41; Katherine Bright 2&#41; Kevin Bright. <BR> <BR>Do any of them overlap? If so, it&#39;s possible &#34;Denny The Dog Catcher&#34; knew them! <BR> <BR>Victor<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10110-->
<!--Post: 10189--><!--Time: 1109803641-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10189"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 2:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kevin Bright- Worked at Coleman from March 1973-June 1973 took one month off for a &#39;vacation&#39; returned to Coleman and resumed the same job he had from July 1973 until August 1973 when he quit for good. <BR>Worked at Coleman during the same time as Dennis Rader from March 1973-June 1973. <BR> Interestingly when Kevin Bright returned to Coleman after his one month vacation in July of 1973 this is the same time that Rader leaves Coleman. <BR> <BR>Kathryn Bright- Worked at Coleman from about January 1972 until her murder. She graduated from high school in June 1971, went to one semester of College probably Fall 1972 September-December 1972 and then quit college and got a job at Coleman. Most likely after Christmas holiday which would be early January 1972. <BR>She worked there during the time Dennis Rader was employed there. <BR> <BR>Julie Otero- She moved to Wichita in the Fall of 1973 and worked at Coleman until being layed off just before her murder in January 1974. <BR>She did not work at Coleman during the time that Dennis Rader worked there.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10189-->
<!--Post: 10202--><!--Time: 1109812713-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10202"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:blingbling1169@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cawichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cawichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 5:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whatthe, don&#39;t forget now, Wichita is not an innocent place. We have had at least 2 sets of quadruple murders in the last few years. Really bad ones, one of which was very highly publicized. I have buried many a friend in Wichita from homicide. People do get murdered in Wichita-a lot!!!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10202-->
<!--Post: 10214--><!--Time: 1109819644-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10214"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 7:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wow, JOHNO, as usual, great work! This is something astounding we haven&#39;t even heard from the cops or news media! <BR> <BR>That means KATHERYN BRIGHT worked at Coleman at the SAME TIME as &#34;Denny The Dog Catcher&#34; Rader from June 19, 1972 to July 6, 1973! A FULL YEAR!! <BR> <BR>KEVIN BRIGHT Worked for Coleman during the SAME TIME as Dennis Rader from March 1973-June 1973 &#40;with some overlap also probably in July 1973&#41;- which is ABOUT 4 MONTHS! <BR> <BR>This is plenty of time for him to have researched &amp; stalked them. However, in defense of L.E., he didn&#39;t kill Katheryn &#40;and almost killed Kevin&#41; untill around 9 months AFTER he left Coleman. This would make it harder for L.E. to peg him. <BR> <BR>Wonder if he was a &#34;disgruntled ex-employee&#34;?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10214-->
<!--Post: 10218--><!--Time: 1109821001-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10218"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 7:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Who as a mere 18 year old kid gets a job and works there for just three months is allowed to take a one month vacation and is rehired to do the same job and then quits one month after being rehired?  <BR>Coincidently, BTK suspect Dennis Rader leaves the job at Coleman where he has been employed for one year at the same time that Kevin Bright returns from his one month vacation. <BR>Something here doesn&#39;t add up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10218-->
<!--Post: 10253--><!--Time: 1109854373-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10253"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 4:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That would be 4 per 100,000 making it even less likely they were unrelated &#40; United States 0.04 per 1000 people&#41; <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10253-->
<!--Post: 10269--><!--Time: 1109866682-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10269"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whatthehell<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whatthehell<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 8:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->STEALTH, <BR> <BR>That is correct thatnks for pointing that out. <BR>I think as time goes buy we will see some connection and maybe the seed that started the killing and turned on the monster. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10269-->
<!--Post: 10354--><!--Time: 1109907461-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10354"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 7:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Your on it Johno! I think Denny was hitting on his sister, Kevin jumped on him for it, Denny swelled up like a dog catcher then intimidated Kevin, Kevin quit. Sis revealed to her supervisor why he quit, DTDC was fired, and Kevin rehired. Which also means there had to be an altercation that Kevin for some reason doesn&#39;t remember.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10354-->
<!--Post: 10355--><!--Time: 1109907732-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10355"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 7:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oh and, Coleman had a sexual harrassment policy even in the early 70&#39;s according to family members! Maybe, Ms. Bright or even Mrs. Otero complained and DTDC was fired.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10355-->
<!--Post: 10535--><!--Time: 1109986013-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10535"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 5:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->News Articles <BR>BTK Said he hadto go to New York and that he did  <BR>not want to hurt them.  <BR>However, he forced Kevin to tie his sister to a chair and then took Kevin to another room, where  <BR>he attempted to bind him.  <BR>The assailant had a cord of some type around Kevin\rquote s neck and was tightening it when Kevin  <BR>fought and was shot twice in the head with a .22-caliber automatic pistol.  <BR>Bright was able to escape and flagged down a passing vehicle. One person in the car took him to  <BR>the hospital while the other summoned police.  <BR>Kathryn was unconscious when officers arrived and died following surgery.  <BR>Police are continuing their investigation into the case and also the Otero murders.  <BR>In the Bright case, they are searching for a white male, 5-foot-11 and about 25 years old. At the time The Wichita Beacon  <BR>April 5, 1974  <BR>By Glenda Holder  <BR> <BR>The victims of a robbery Thursday afternoon, a 20-year-old woman who was fatally stabbed and  <BR>her 19-year-old brother who was shot in the head, were employees of the Coleman Co., as were victims  <BR>of two other recent violent crimes.  <BR> <BR>Kathryn D. Bright, died about five hours after she was stabbed three times in the abdomen by the intruder  <BR>in her home at 3217 E. 13th.  <BR> <BR>Kevin Bright, who accompanied his sister to her home, received two gunshot wounds to the head after  <BR>he opposed the man. He was listed in serious condition at Wesley Medical Center today.  <BR> <BR>Mrs. Joseph Ortero, who along with Kathryn became an employee of the company in August 1973 and was  <BR>still employed by the firm.  <BR>Kevin, of Valley Center, began working for Coleman in March 1973 and quit in June to take a vacation.  <BR>Records show he was rehired to do the same job in July and quit in August.  <BR> <BR>Mrs. Joseph Otero, who along with three other members of her family were brutally slain Jan. 15, was  <BR>employed at Coleman as an assembler from the middle of December to the first part of January. Miss  <BR>Bright had worked as an assembler since March 11. Prior to that time she had worked as a brazer.  <BR>A supervisor of assembly, Michael L. Williams, 26, was shot in the abdomen Jan. 12 by two unknown  <BR>persons who apparently were attempting to rob him at him home in 4140 N. Battin. He was shot when  <BR>the assailants fired shotgun blasts through the door.  <BR>On March 28 someone broke into Williams&#39; home and took a rifle and a radio. When laboratory  <BR>investigators arrived at the scene, they were unable to obtain fingerprints because Williams had touched  <BR>the surface the burglar had touched.  <BR>Police Chief Floyd Hannon is the only officer issuing statements concerning the Thursday homicide.  <BR>However, he was attending a class this morning and could not be contacted about the case or any possible  <BR>connection with the Otero or Williams incidents.  <BR>Drugs also have been mentioned in the Williams and Otero cases, but neither police nor sheriff&#39;s  <BR>officers, who are investigating the Williams shooting, have been able to rule out or confirm this possibility.  <BR>The Beacon learned that a quantity of unknown drugs was found by police in the Bright home.  <BR>The killer apparently broke a glass in the backdoor of the east Wichita residence and waited in a backroom  <BR>for Kathryn and Kevin.  <BR>The two returned to the residence about 2 p.m. and were confronted by the man, police at the  <BR>scene said.  <BR>He allegedly told the couple that he wanted money and their car <BR>of the crime, he was wearing a black stocking cap and an orange shirt and jacket. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>Chief Denies Coleman Link In Slayings  <BR> <BR>The Wichita Beacon  <BR>April 8, 1974  <BR>&#40;no reporter name given&#41;  <BR> <BR>Police Chief Floyd Hannon said today there is no connection between the Jan. 15 murders of the  <BR>Joseph Otero family and a quadruple murder last week in Portland, Ore.  <BR> <BR>Hannon also told reporters at City Hall a remark by an officer last week connecting the Otero murders  <BR>and other incidents to the Coleman Co. should not have been made.  <BR> <BR>The remark resulted in a story relating employment at Coleman by Mrs. Otero; Kathryn Bright,  <BR>who was stabbed to death Thursday, and Michael L. Williams, who was shot and wounded Jan. 12.  <BR> <BR>Hannon said any innuendo a place of business is involved in the drug traffic should not have been made.  <BR> <BR>Police have been investigating a possible connection between the violence and drug trafficking.  <BR> <BR>A story in The Wichita Beacon, however, did not actually connect the Coleman Co. to the incidents  <BR>but merely showed the victims had been employed there where they may have developed common acquaintances.  <BR> <BR>Hannon said today there had been about 12 cases of violence since November that also may be connected.  <BR> <BR>He said the victims of those represent a cross-section of the community - &#34; so we can&#39;t look at Coleman.&#34;  <BR> <BR>Hannon did not comment further on why the Portland connection has been eliminated.  <BR> <BR>That crime resulted in the deaths of Howard A. Weeks, his wife, Arlene, and two boys for whom  <BR>they babysat.  <BR> <BR>As in the Otero murders, the crime took place in early morning daylight at the home and the victims  <BR>were bound and gagged similarly. Also, a description of a suspect seen leaving the Week&#39;s home  <BR>was similar to a description of a suspect seen leaving the Otero home. <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10535-->
<!--Post: 10757--><!--Time: 1110212849-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10757"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whatthehell<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whatthehell<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 8:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Embersage,  <BR>  <BR>Are you sayin that there is no connection. <BR>It sure seems the further along we go the more likelyhood that there is a connection. The statistics are amazingly high for it to be just coincedence. I think we will learn alot of amazing thing that non of us ever thought of as the story plays out.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10757-->
<!--Post: 10821--><!--Time: 1110241983-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10821"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 4:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Damn near everyone seemed to have worked at Coleman but Boeing, Cessna, Beechcraft&#40;Ratheon&#41;,Leerjet nor any of the hundreds of support companies that supply parts and avionics to the aircraft industry seem to pop up. This hardly seems like a cross-section of the population of the Air Capital City.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
