<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11479"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 9:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B- In the 70&#39;s Boeing started cutting it&#39;s production line down in the military department <BR>and started laying off those who built bombers. Some of them were transfered to Seattle etc. It would have made a difference for the cross section of population in Wichita.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11479-->
<!--Post: 11486--><!--Time: 1110781833-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11486"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 10:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->But what I am saying is that a significant number of people involved in the killings including the killer had worked for coleman while I&#39;m not hearing of any reports that any of them were working for aircraft manufactures. During that year the national average for murder victims was 4 people for every 10000 of population while during that same year the average for coleman employees was nearly 7/10000 victims vs population &#40;and thats not counting the 3 extra victims that were collateral damage&#41;. <BR> <BR>&#40;A special thanks to Whatthehell&#39;s march 1 post above for statistical link and information&#41; <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
